{# THE action bar for a sell-side document — the order's, the quote's and the invoice's, once.

   Three near-identical <nav>s stood here before this: `admin/order/_tab_nav.html.twig`,
   `admin/estimate/_tab_nav.html.twig` and `admin/invoice/_tab_nav.html.twig`, each with its own
   copy of the View tab, the PDF tab, the right-aligned PDF/Download disclosure and (on the order
   alone) an overflow menu. The genuinely common set measured three items — View, the document's
   own PDF, and one related-document link — and the shape around them was copied three times, which
   is why Clone reached one document of three and Lock reached none at all.

   ## The rule this partial is built on

   PARAMETERS, NEVER `{% if document == 'invoice' %}`. Nothing below asks which document it is
   rendering. Every difference between the three arrives as a value or as a TEMPLATE PATH, the same
   way `sales_detail_line_table.html.twig` takes its Actions cell and its <tfoot>. A difference that
   cannot be expressed that way belongs in the calling `_tab_nav`, not in a branch here.

   ## The shape

       Bar       View · Edit · <own PDF> · [barTemplate] · PDF / Download ▾ · ⋯
       Overflow  [overflowTemplate] · Clone · Delete · Lock / Unlock

   which is the owner's Zoho reference with the names this application actually has. Two of that
   reference's items are deliberately absent: **Share**, which has no route anywhere, and
   **Preferences**, which is out of scope. **Email** is not shared either — `admin_invoice_send` is
   the only mail route on the sell side — so it stays in the invoice's own print-menu slot.

   ## No JavaScript

   Both disclosures are `<details>`/`<summary>`, not the `.row-action-toggle` button the row grids
   use. That button is inert with scripting off — app.js:4254 is the only thing that opens the
   panel, by copying its HTML into a body-level clone — so a menu built on it hides its contents
   from a no-JS browser entirely, and this bar is where Clone, Lock and Send Invoice live. Core
   already answers this: `admin/_row_actions_no_js.html.twig` is the same dropdown as a native
   disclosure, keeping `.row-action-dropdown` so the styling is core's and not a second copy. It is
   included once, here, because this bar is included once per page.

   A second gain from `<details>`: app.js's clone duplicates every id inside a panel it opens. A
   disclosure it never touches keeps this bar's ids unique, which is what lets a test anchor to one
   (#627).

   ## Delete

   The control is rendered and is DEAD, by instruction. No `admin_order_delete`,
   `admin_estimate_delete` or `admin_invoice_delete` route exists and none is in scope. It is a
   `<button disabled>` — the only control in HTML that cannot be activated by mouse, keyboard or
   form submit, and which carries no href to land on a 404 — dimmed with the three declarations
   core's own `.button.is-disabled` uses (that class cannot be borrowed directly: `.button` inside
   `.company-action-links` restyles it as a bar tab). `data-inert` says why, in the markup.

   Parameters
   ----------
   document          required  the entity. Read for ONE thing: `document_is_locked()` /
                               `document_lock()`. Not branched on.
   idPrefix          required  'order' | 'quote' | 'invoice'. Every control's id is
                               `{idPrefix}-action-{name}`, so a test names an element instead of
                               see()ing a bare word like "Edit" or "Lock" (#627).
   documentNoun      required  'order' | 'quote' | 'invoice' — the word the shared labels read
                               with ("Clone Order", "Lock this invoice").
   ariaLabel         required  the <nav>'s accessible name.
   navClass          optional  extra classes on the <nav>. The invoice passes 'no-print'.
   view              required  {href, current} — the View tab.
   edit              optional  {href, label} or null. NULL RENDERS NO EDIT CONTROL, which is how
                               a document whose own state machine withholds editing right now says
                               so — an issued invoice or one that bills an order, a locked document,
                               an accepted quote.
   pdf               optional  {href, label, current} or null. NULL RENDERS NO PDF CONTROL, the
                               same convention `edit` uses — for a document whose own PDF is
                               already reachable another way in this same bar (the order's
                               printMenuTemplate offers the identical route as "Print Sales
                               Order"). Quote and Invoice always pass one today.
   barTemplate       optional  template path rendered in the bar after the fixed set: this
                               document's own bar actions.
   barContext        optional  extra variables for barTemplate. `document` is always passed.
   printMenuTemplate optional  template path rendered inside the shared PDF / Download disclosure.
   printContext      optional  extra variables for printMenuTemplate.
   overflowTemplate  optional  template path rendered at the TOP of the ⋯ overflow: this document's
                               own secondary actions. No document supplies one today — see the
                               report for the three Zoho puts there and why none of them moved.
   overflowContext   optional  extra variables for overflowTemplate.
   cloneUrl          required  POST target for Clone.
   lockUrl           required  POST target for Lock.
   unlockUrl         required  POST target for Unlock.
#}
{% include 'admin/_row_actions_no_js.html.twig' %}
{% set barLocked = document_is_locked(document) %}
{% set barLockRow = barLocked ? document_lock(document) : null %}
<nav class="company-action-links order-tab-nav{{ navClass|default('') != '' ? ' ' ~ navClass : '' }}" aria-label="{{ ariaLabel }}">
    <a id="{{ idPrefix }}-action-view" class="button{{ view.current|default(false) ? ' is-current' : '' }}" href="{{ view.href }}">View</a>
    {# Absent, not disabled, when the caller passes null. The three documents withhold it for three
       different reasons and each works that out for itself — see the calling _tab_nav. #}
    {% if edit|default(null) is not null %}
        <a id="{{ idPrefix }}-action-edit" class="button" href="{{ edit.href }}">{{ edit.label }}</a>
    {% endif %}
    {# Absent, not disabled, when the caller passes null — same convention as `edit` above. #}
    {% if pdf|default(null) is not null %}
        <a id="{{ idPrefix }}-action-pdf" class="button{{ pdf.current|default(false) ? ' is-current' : '' }}" href="{{ pdf.href }}">{{ pdf.label }}</a>
    {% endif %}
    {% if barTemplate|default(null) is not null %}
        {% include barTemplate with {document: document}|merge(barContext|default({})) only %}
    {% endif %}
    {# `no-js-row-actions--overlay`: this bar sits in normal panel flow with nothing clipping it —
       unlike the row grids `_row_actions_no_js.html.twig` also serves, there is no
       `.table-scroll-region` here to reparent the panel out from under — so both of this bar's
       disclosures opt into the FLOATING variant instead of the in-flow default. See that
       partial's docblock for why the default is in-flow at all.

       Kept in the same left-aligned cluster as every other tab now, not pushed to the far right —
       a bar with two or three tabs used to leave a wide dead gap before it. #}
    <details class="row-action-menu no-js-row-actions no-js-row-actions--overlay">
        {# `.btn-pdf order-pdf-toggle` and NOT `.row-action-toggle`: the two former classes are the
           whole of this control's look (app.css:5083, 12620), and the last is the hook app.js
           binds to — a <summary> carrying it would open natively AND be cloned to the body. The
           chevron came from `.row-action-toggle::after`, so it is written out here instead. #}
        <summary id="{{ idPrefix }}-action-print-menu" class="btn-pdf order-pdf-toggle" aria-label="PDF and download options">PDF / Download ▾</summary>
        <div class="row-action-dropdown company-action-dropdown">
            {% if printMenuTemplate|default(null) is not null %}
                {% include printMenuTemplate with {document: document}|merge(printContext|default({})) only %}
            {% endif %}
        </div>
    </details>
    <details class="row-action-menu no-js-row-actions no-js-row-actions--overlay">
        <summary id="{{ idPrefix }}-action-more" class="mini-action" aria-label="More {{ documentNoun }} actions">&hellip;</summary>
        <div class="row-action-dropdown company-action-dropdown">
            {% if overflowTemplate|default(null) is not null %}
                {% include overflowTemplate with {document: document}|merge(overflowContext|default({})) only %}
            {% endif %}
            {# Offered on a LOCKED document too, and that is deliberate and tested: a lock freezes
               what the document IS, and the clone is a different document. DocumentLockService's
               docblock and DocumentCloneAndLockCest both say so in those words. #}
            <form id="{{ idPrefix }}-action-clone-form" method="post" action="{{ cloneUrl }}" style="display: contents;">
                {{ csrf_field() }}
                <button id="{{ idPrefix }}-action-clone" type="submit">Clone {{ documentNoun|capitalize }}</button>
            </form>
            <button id="{{ idPrefix }}-action-delete" class="danger" type="button" disabled
                    data-inert="no-delete-route"
                    style="opacity: 0.6; cursor: not-allowed; pointer-events: none;">Delete</button>
            <span class="row-action-divider"></span>
            {% if barLocked %}
                <span id="{{ idPrefix }}-action-lock-state">Locked by {{ barLockRow.locked_by }}{% if barLockRow.reason %} — {{ barLockRow.reason }}{% endif %}</span>
                {# Lock is any admin, unlock is ROLE_SUPER_ADMIN — asymmetric on purpose, see
                   DocumentLockService. ROLE_TECH_SUPPORT inherits it. An admin who cannot unlock is
                   told who to ask rather than shown a button that answers 403. #}
                {% if is_granted('ROLE_SUPER_ADMIN') %}
                    <form id="{{ idPrefix }}-action-unlock-form" method="post" action="{{ unlockUrl }}" style="display: contents;">
                        {{ csrf_field() }}
                        <button id="{{ idPrefix }}-action-unlock" type="submit">Unlock {{ documentNoun|capitalize }}</button>
                    </form>
                {% else %}
                    <span id="{{ idPrefix }}-action-unlock-denied">Only a super admin can unlock this {{ documentNoun }}.</span>
                {% endif %}
            {% else %}
                {# Opens the hidden lock modal below (app.js, `.js-lock-modal-open`). The reason field and
                   submit live in a real <form method="post"> in that modal, so a browser without
                   JavaScript — or a test — can still submit it directly. #}
                <button id="{{ idPrefix }}-action-lock" type="button" class="js-lock-modal-open">Lock {{ documentNoun|capitalize }}</button>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
    </details>
</nav>
{% if not barLocked %}
    <div class="modal-backdrop lock-modal" hidden>
        <form class="modal-card" method="post" id="{{ idPrefix }}-action-lock-form" action="{{ lockUrl }}" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="{{ idPrefix }}-lock-modal-title">
            {{ csrf_field() }}
            <h2 id="{{ idPrefix }}-lock-modal-title">Lock {{ documentNoun|capitalize }}</h2>
            <label class="note-modal-field">
                Reason (optional)
                <input id="{{ idPrefix }}-action-lock-reason" type="text" name="reason" maxlength="255" aria-label="Reason this {{ documentNoun }} is locked">
            </label>
            <div class="modal-actions">
                <button class="button outline js-lock-modal-close" type="button">Cancel</button>
                <button class="button primary" type="submit">Lock {{ documentNoun|capitalize }}</button>
            </div>
        </form>
    </div>
{% endif %}
